# Copy to mobile/.env and set the API URL for your machine.
#
# A physical device cannot reach the development machine's localhost, so this must
# be the machine's LAN address, not 127.0.0.1. Find it with `ipconfig` on Windows
# (IPv4 Address on your active adapter) or `ifconfig` on macOS and Linux.
#
# Both the phone and the development machine must be on the same network, and
# Windows Firewall must allow inbound TCP on the port.
#
# THIS VALUE IS BAKED INTO THE BUNDLE AT BUILD TIME. EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables are
# inlined by the bundler, so a release build carries whatever the machine that
# built it had set here. A release built on a development machine would ship
# pointing at a laptop on somebody's wifi.
#
# The app refuses that: a production build requires an https URL on a public
# host, and fails at the first request with an explanation if it gets a LAN,
# loopback or link-local address. Build releases from CI or from a machine with
# the production value set, and never from a working development checkout.
#
# Nothing secret belongs here. EXPO_PUBLIC_ values are readable by anyone with
# the app, so this base URL is the only backend configuration the app holds.
# Payment happens on the provider's hosted page and the app never sees a Paystack
# key of any kind.

EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.24:8000
